{
  "description": "Contextual auditing for control-plane modules (Issue #45.2). Verifies that system.control.* modules include caller_id and a redacted identity snapshot in their emitted audit events, defaulting caller_id to '@external' when the caller is unauthenticated. The bare-substring case added for D-93 (spec v1.50.0) is the one that discriminates: the pre-existing bearer_token case is caught by every spelling of the list, which is why a credential leak in one SDK passed this fixture for as long as it did.",
  "test_cases": [
    {
      "id": "update_config_with_caller_id",
      "description": "When context.caller_id is set, the apcore.config.updated event payload MUST include that caller_id verbatim.",
      "module_id": "system.control.update_config",
      "context": {
        "caller_id": "ops.console",
        "identity": null
      },
      "input": {
        "key": "executor.default_timeout",
        "value": 60000,
        "reason": "increase timeout"
      },
      "expected": {
        "event_type": "apcore.config.updated",
        "data_contains": {
          "key": "executor.default_timeout",
          "old_value": 30000,
          "new_value": 60000,
          "caller_id": "ops.console"
        },
        "data_must_not_contain_keys": [
          "identity"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "update_config_external_default",
      "description": "When context.caller_id is null/empty, the audit event payload caller_id MUST default to the literal string '@external'.",
      "module_id": "system.control.update_config",
      "context": {
        "caller_id": null,
        "identity": null
      },
      "input": {
        "key": "executor.default_timeout",
        "value": 60000,
        "reason": "increase timeout"
      },
      "expected": {
        "event_type": "apcore.config.updated",
        "data_contains": {
          "caller_id": "@external"
        },
        "data_must_not_contain_keys": [
          "identity"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "update_config_empty_string_caller_external_default",
      "description": "An empty-string caller_id MUST be treated as unauthenticated and defaulted to '@external'.",
      "module_id": "system.control.update_config",
      "context": {
        "caller_id": "",
        "identity": null
      },
      "input": {
        "key": "executor.default_timeout",
        "value": 60000,
        "reason": "increase timeout"
      },
      "expected": {
        "event_type": "apcore.config.updated",
        "data_contains": {
          "caller_id": "@external"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "toggle_feature_includes_identity",
      "description": "When context.identity is set, the apcore.module.toggled event MUST include a redacted identity snapshot (id, type, optional display_name).",
      "module_id": "system.control.toggle_feature",
      "context": {
        "caller_id": "user-42",
        "identity": {
          "id": "user-42",
          "type": "user",
          "display_name": "alice@example.com"
        }
      },
      "input": {
        "module_id": "risky.module",
        "enabled": false,
        "reason": "incident-1234"
      },
      "expected": {
        "event_type": "apcore.module.toggled",
        "data_contains": {
          "module_id": "risky.module",
          "enabled": false,
          "caller_id": "user-42",
          "identity": {
            "id": "user-42",
            "type": "user",
            "display_name": "alice@example.com"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "toggle_feature_redacts_sensitive_identity_fields",
      "description": "Identity fields marked x-sensitive (e.g., bearer_token) MUST be replaced with '<redacted>' in the audit event payload.",
      "module_id": "system.control.toggle_feature",
      "context": {
        "caller_id": "service-bot",
        "identity": {
          "id": "service-bot",
          "type": "service",
          "bearer_token": "secret-abc-123"
        }
      },
      "input": {
        "module_id": "risky.module",
        "enabled": true,
        "reason": "rollback"
      },
      "expected": {
        "event_type": "apcore.module.toggled",
        "data_contains": {
          "caller_id": "service-bot",
          "identity": {
            "id": "service-bot",
            "type": "service",
            "bearer_token": "<redacted>"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "reload_module_includes_caller_and_identity",
      "description": "system.control.reload_module MUST include caller_id + identity in apcore.module.reloaded events.",
      "module_id": "system.control.reload_module",
      "context": {
        "caller_id": "deploy-bot",
        "identity": {
          "id": "deploy-bot",
          "type": "service"
        }
      },
      "input": {
        "module_id": "executor.email.send",
        "reason": "hotfix"
      },
      "expected": {
        "event_type": "apcore.module.reloaded",
        "data_contains": {
          "module_id": "executor.email.send",
          "caller_id": "deploy-bot",
          "identity": {
            "id": "deploy-bot",
            "type": "service"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "audit_event_emitted_without_audit_store",
      "description": "Even when no AuditStore is configured, the audit event MUST still be emitted on the event bus with caller_id populated.",
      "module_id": "system.control.update_config",
      "context": {
        "caller_id": "ops.console",
        "identity": null
      },
      "audit_store": null,
      "input": {
        "key": "executor.default_timeout",
        "value": 60000,
        "reason": "increase timeout"
      },
      "expected": {
        "event_type": "apcore.config.updated",
        "data_contains": {
          "caller_id": "ops.console"
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "toggle_feature_redacts_bare_substring_identity_fields",
      "description": "The identity redaction list matches on BARE substrings -- key, auth, session -- not on an enumeration of compounds. The three attributes here discriminate between the two: signing_key contains none of api_key/apikey/access_key/private_key; auth_header does not contain authorization; session_id matches nothing in a compound list. apcore-typescript enumerated compounds and published all three verbatim to every subscriber, log sink and audit store on the event bus, while apcore-python and apcore-rust redacted them (D-93). The existing bearer_token case cannot see this: every list catches it. The list is deliberately a superset of obs.redaction.sensitive_keys so credentials cannot leak here even when global redaction is off. API-Key is included cased and hyphenated because the match is case-insensitive and substring-based, not an equality test against a known spelling.",
      "module_id": "system.control.toggle_feature",
      "context": {
        "caller_id": "service-bot",
        "identity": {
          "id": "service-bot",
          "type": "service",
          "signing_key": "MIIEvQIBADANBgkq",
          "auth_header": "Basic dXNlcjpwdw==",
          "session_id": "s-abc123",
          "API-Key": "sk-live-1",
          "tenant": "acme"
        }
      },
      "input": {
        "module_id": "risky.module",
        "enabled": true,
        "reason": "rollback"
      },
      "expected": {
        "event_type": "apcore.module.toggled",
        "data_contains": {
          "caller_id": "service-bot",
          "identity": {
            "id": "service-bot",
            "type": "service",
            "signing_key": "<redacted>",
            "auth_header": "<redacted>",
            "session_id": "<redacted>",
            "API-Key": "<redacted>",
            "tenant": "acme"
          }
        }
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "toggle_feature_omits_an_empty_roles_list_from_the_identity_snapshot",
      "description": "D-118: an identity carrying `roles: []` produces an audit snapshot with NO `roles` key. The spec names only `id`, `type` and optionally `display_name`. Asserting `roles: []` would NOT discriminate \u2014 that is exactly what the diverging SDK emits, and `data_contains` is a SUBSET match, so an extra key passes it. The assertion has to be key ABSENCE, which is why this case needs `identity_must_not_contain_keys` rather than a richer `data_contains`.",
      "module_id": "system.control.toggle_feature",
      "context": {
        "caller_id": "user-77",
        "identity": {
          "id": "user-77",
          "type": "user",
          "roles": []
        }
      },
      "input": {
        "module_id": "risky.module",
        "enabled": false,
        "reason": "incident-2345"
      },
      "expected": {
        "event_type": "apcore.module.toggled",
        "data_contains": {
          "caller_id": "user-77",
          "identity": {
            "id": "user-77",
            "type": "user"
          }
        },
        "identity_must_not_contain_keys": [
          "roles"
        ]
      }
    },
    {
      "id": "toggle_feature_keeps_a_non_empty_roles_list",
      "description": "The control for the case above. Without it, an SDK that simply never emits `roles` passes \u2014 and the decision is about the EMPTY list only.",
      "module_id": "system.control.toggle_feature",
      "context": {
        "caller_id": "user-88",
        "identity": {
          "id": "user-88",
          "type": "user",
          "roles": [
            "analyst"
          ]
        }
      },
      "input": {
        "module_id": "risky.module",
        "enabled": true,
        "reason": "restore"
      },
      "expected": {
        "event_type": "apcore.module.toggled",
        "data_contains": {
          "caller_id": "user-88",
          "identity": {
            "id": "user-88",
            "type": "user",
            "roles": [
              "analyst"
            ]
          }
        }
      }
    }
  ]
}
